	Hope this isn't dull. Not what I'd call a spoiler, but just in case...

	Anyway, I always identify a few gems (shake out the glass in a box, then
identify the rest with a blessed scroll of identify). Then when I visit the
Gnomish Mall, I sell a good gem, then a few things until the storekeeper is out
of money. At that point he gives you credit, which means he "pays" you about
twice as much or more zorkmids for each item as he pays cash, in fact, giving
you about his selling price.
	Then when I collect junk around the mall, I sell it to the general store
shop for credit until I have a lot (usually I go up and down, finding wraiths
or vampires or wights to lower my level so I can armor up (AM I THE ONLY PERSON
WHO DOES THIS WITH PRIESTS? PROBABLY NOT, BUT THOSE WHO HAVEN'T THOUGHT OF IT,
TRY IT!!! JUST DON'T GO BELOW LEVEL 1. THEN PAY {CHEAPLY} THE PRIEST(ESS) EVEN
WORKS WITH NON-COALIGNED PRIESTS, I THINK. RAISES ARMOR).
	At long last, the point:
	
     I kick all the items out of the TOOL shop INTO the general store. This
does NOT make the shopkeeper either angry or after me for money!!! It is all
in the family. In this way, a little junk collecting earned me all the toolshop
items. What I didn't need, I sold back. If any two other shops are next to each
other (door to door) that would work too, but you would need stuff to sell to
one. OF COURSE, THIS DOES NOT WORK WITH BREAKABLE ITEMS, CAMERAS, MIRRORS, ETC.

     This is one of the pleasantest ways to rob a shop I know. *Kick* #chat
with keeper "... talks about the problem of shoplifting." I know what you mean,
you say, sympathetically. *Kick* *Kick*

